          "grounding_supports": [
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 85,
                "end_index": 270,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Instead, they determine them with extreme accuracy using **iterative algorithms**\u2014mathematical procedures that start with a rough guess and rapidly refine it to reach the exact answer"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 274,
                "end_index": 477,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because computers operate in binary and can perform billions of calculations per second, they can run these refinement loops until they hit the physical limits of precision in a fraction of a microsecond"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 772,
                "end_index": 904,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Fortunately, computers store numbers using the **IEEE 754 floating-point standard**, which is essentially binary scientific notation"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 970,
                "end_index": 1053,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because of this format, finding a great starting guess is mathematically simplified"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1058,
                "end_index": 1209,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "**The Exponent:** The computer takes the exponent and divides it by $2$ (which in binary is done instantly by shifting the bits one space to the right)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1214,
                "end_index": 1364,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "**The Mantissa:** The computer uses a small, built-in \"lookup table\" in its processor to find a rough approximation of the square root of the mantissa"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1367,
                "end_index": 1450,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This gives the computer an incredibly accurate starting guess in a single CPU cycle"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1465,
                "end_index": 1629,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Refining the Guess: Newton\u2019s Method\nOnce the computer has a starting guess ($x_0$), it uses **Newton's Method** (also known as the Babylonian Method) to refine it"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2361,
                "end_index": 2528,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because the precision doubles with every step, a computer only needs to run this loop **3 or 4 times** to get an answer that is perfectly accurate to 16 decimal places"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2543,
                "end_index": 2674,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Modern CPU Optimization: Goldschmidt's Algorithm\nWhile Newton's Method is incredibly fast, it requires **division** ($S / x_{old}$)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2676,
                "end_index": 2741,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "In computer chip design, division is a notoriously slow operation"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                8,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2745,
                "end_index": 2871,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "To bypass this bottleneck, modern computer processors (like Intel, AMD, and ARM chips) often use **Goldschmidt\u2019s Algorithm**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2874,
                "end_index": 2988,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Instead of calculating the square root directly, the processor computes the **inverse square root** ($1/\\sqrt{S}$)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
